= Arbitrage — Simple =

Arbitrage tries to profit when the same or economically equivalent thing has inconsistent prices in different places. Real arbitrage still faces fees, timing, capital, and execution risk.

'''Important boundary:''' arbitrage ≠ ordinary speculation.

== Sources ==
* Stephen A. Ross, “The Arbitrage Theory of Capital Asset Pricing” (1976), for no-arbitrage foundations.
* Andrei Shleifer & Robert Vishny, “The Limits of Arbitrage” (1997).
